{"episodes":{"174668":"Storm force west winds developed on portions of Lake Superior from the evening of the 6th into the morning of the 7th in the wake of a strong cold frontal passage.","175408":"A very wet and unsettled pattern affected the islands on the first weekend of November. The trough was on the most favorable position for shower development on November 4th, increasing instability aloft. A surface low was induced, causing winds to shift from the south. As a result, a significant flux of moisture was observed. An organized event of rain and thunderstorms was detected, affecting, once again, the south, east and central regions of Puerto Rico. These rains, along with previous rainfalls during the fall months, resulted in numerous reports of mudslides, flooding and rivers overflowing."},"events":[{"begin":"2022-11-06T00:00Z","county":"Juana Diaz","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.40K","deaths":0,"end":"2022-11-06T00:00Z","endLat":18.0811,"endLon":-66.4989,"episode":175408,"id":1067479,"injuries":0,"lat":18.08,"location":"3.7 NNW Juana Diaz","lon":-66.5,"narrative":"Flooding was reported at road PR-149, before the entrance to Barrio Guayabal. There was one person trapped in their car.","source":"State Official","state":"PR","type":"Flash Flood","wfo":"SJU"},{"begin":"2022-11-06T00:08Z","county":"Rincon","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"10.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2022-11-06T00:08Z","endLat":18.3257,"endLon":-67.249,"episode":175408,"id":1067480,"injuries":0,"lat":18.3254,"location":"1.33 WSW Rincon","lon":-67.2498,"narrative":"Flooding was reported at road 8, near Saffron Sunset Beachfront hotel, a house was affected.","source":"State Official","state":"PR","type":"Flash Flood","wfo":"SJU"},{"begin":"2022-11-06T00:09Z","county":"Fajardo","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"10.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2022-11-06T00:09Z","endLat":18.3345,"endLon":-65.6369,"episode":175408,"id":1067481,"injuries":0,"lat":18.3345,"location":"1.14 NNE Fajardo","lon":